<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Zhovti Vody</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1648">1648</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmelnytsky-uprising">Khmelnytsky Uprising</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Zhovti Vody was fought in April and May 1648 in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, the first major battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmelnytsky-uprising">Khmelnytsky Uprising</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohdan-khmelnytsky">Bohdan Khmelnytsky</a>, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-tatars">Crimean Tatars</a> under Tugay Bey, destroyed an advance force of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> led by Stefan Potocki, after registered Cossacks in Polish service went over to the rebels. A second victory at Korsun followed days later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-zhovti-vody.jpg" alt="Battle of Zhovti Vody" width="320" height="344" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alex Tora · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bytwa_pid_Zhovtymy_Vodamy.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
